2. **Make the first four boards prove the game�?Ts range.** Keep the authored sequence. Aim for the first carrier departure within ten seconds, make both Level 2 bench cats visibly wake up when their carrier arrives, and pulse the exit that the Level 3 kitten frees. At Level 4, watch whether new players choose the earlier carrier unaided. Track Level 4 starts and Level 10 reach.

3. **Make the next move readable on a crowded board.** On press, connect the cat�?Ts exit, first blocker, and projected destination. Use the same pattern symbol on the cat and its carrier. Flag the final free cushion. Keep chain text clear of the carrier mouth, and give tutorial copy and status messages one shared lane. Level 12 already shows what happens when both speak at once.

4. **Make wins fast and losses teach.** Give ordinary clears a compact result with one thumb-level action, **Next** or **Build** when the upgrade is ready. Let the earned star fly into the build meter. On failure, keep the bench and queue visible, point to the overflowing cat, and say how far away its carrier is. Keep **Take back** and **Retry** clear of the life-loss toast.

